---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.tsx";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import CompanyCards from "../components/CompanyCards.astro";
---

<Layout title="About — Halvard Mørstad">
  <PageHeader current="about" />

  <!-- Hero -->
  <div class="mb-6" style="padding-right: 40px;">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 mb-1">
      <h1 class="font-medium m-0 text-heading" style="font-size: 1.25rem;">
        Halvard Mørstad
      </h1>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <a
          href="https://github.com/lmxrd"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          aria-label="GitHub"
        >
          <Icon name="brand-github" size={16} color="var(--color-dim)" />
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/halvard-mørstad-4b8b13144/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          aria-label="LinkedIn"
        >
          <Icon name="brand-linkedin" size={16} color="var(--color-dim)" />
        </a>
        <a href="mailto:jobs@morstad.eu" aria-label="Email">
          <Icon name="mail" size={16} color="var(--color-dim)" />
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="m-0 text-muted text-xs mb-2">
      Principal Engineer | Cloud & Infrastructure | Fractional CTO
    </p>
    <p class="m-0 text-muted" style="font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.7;">
      I help founders and business leaders turn ideas into working software,
      without needing a technical team in place yet.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- CTA buttons -->
  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2.5 mb-8">
    <a
      href="mailto:jobs@morstad.eu"
      class="btn-primary"
      style="padding: 0.5rem 1rem; font-size: 0.8125rem; display: inline-flex; align-items: center;"
    >
      Get in touch
    </a>
    <a
      href="/work"
      class="btn-outline"
      style="padding: 0.5rem 0.875rem; font-size: 0.8125rem; display: inline-flex; align-items: center;"
    >
      View my work
    </a>
    <a
      href="/blog"
      class="btn-outline"
      style="padding: 0.5rem 0.875rem; font-size: 0.8125rem; display: inline-flex; align-items: center;"
    >
      Check out my blog
    </a>
  </div>

  <!-- Link back to technical version -->
  <a
    href="/"
    class="btn-outline"
    style="padding: 0.625rem 1.125rem; font-size: 0.8125rem; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.625rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; text-decoration: none;"
  >
    <Icon name="click" size={20} color="var(--color-link)" />
    <span>Are you a developer? See the technical version here</span>
  </a>

  <!-- The problem -->
  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="m-0 mb-2 text-dim" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">
      The problem I solve
    </h2>
    <p class="m-0 text-muted" style="font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.8;">
      You have a vision, a market, maybe even early customers. What you need is
      someone who can build the product, make the right technical decisions, and
      eventually hand it off to a team. Hiring a full engineering team on day
      one is expensive and risky. You need someone who can take you from "this
      is what we want to build" to "this is how we build it".
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- How I can help -->
  <section
    class="mb-8"
    style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); padding-top: 1.25rem;"
  >
    <h2 class="m-0 mb-2.5 text-dim" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">
      How I can help
    </h2>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <article class="card" style="padding: 1rem;">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-1.5">
          <Icon name="code" size={16} color="#85b7eb" />
          <h3 class="font-medium m-0 text-heading" style="font-size: 0.875rem;">
            Your technical co-founder
          </h3>
        </div>
        <p
          class="m-0 text-muted"
          style="font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.7;"
        >
          I build the first version of your product myself, frontend, backend,
          and everything in between. You get a working product to show investors
          and customers without hiring a team first. When the time comes to
          scale, I help you hire and onboard your first engineers.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card" style="padding: 1rem;">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-1.5">
          <Icon name="bulb" size={16} color="#f0997b" />
          <h3 class="font-medium m-0 text-heading" style="font-size: 0.875rem;">
            Your interim CTO
          </h3>
        </div>
        <p
          class="m-0 text-muted"
          style="font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.7;"
        >
          If you already have a team but no technical leader, I step in to set
          direction, establish processes, and make sure the engineering is on
          track. I stay until you've found the right permanent hire, then I hand
          over cleanly.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card" style="padding: 1rem;">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-1.5">
          <Icon name="users" size={16} color="#97c459" />
          <h3 class="font-medium m-0 text-heading" style="font-size: 0.875rem;">
            Your technical advisor
          </h3>
        </div>
        <p
          class="m-0 text-muted"
          style="font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.7;"
        >
          Sometimes you just need a second opinion. I help you evaluate whether
          your current setup makes sense, what to build next, and whether you're
          spending money on the right things. No commitment, no retainer, just
          straight answers.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What it's like to work with me -->
  <section
    class="mt-8 mb-8"
    style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); padding-top: 1.25rem;"
  >
    <h2 class="m-0 mb-3 text-dim text-xs">What it's like to work with me</h2>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <p class="m-0 text-muted" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.7;">
        <span class="text-dim">I speak human, not jargon. </span>You'll always
        know what we're building, why, and what it costs. No surprise bills or
        mysterious technical debt.
      </p>
      <p class="m-0 text-muted" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.7;">
        <span class="text-dim">I build things that last. </span>The product I
        hand you isn't a prototype held together with tape. It's something your
        future team can understand, maintain, and build on.
      </p>
      <p class="m-0 text-muted" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.7;">
        <span class="text-dim">I'm honest about what you need. </span>If
        something isn't worth building, I'll tell you before you pay for it.
      </p>
      <p class="m-0 text-muted" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.7;">
        <span class="text-dim">I mentor the people I work with. </span>If you
        have junior developers, I'll grow them. If you don't have a team yet,
        I'll help you hire one.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- On AI -->
  <section
    class="mb-8"
    style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); padding-top: 1.25rem;"
  >
    <h2 class="m-0 mb-2 text-dim" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">On AI</h2>
    <p class="m-0 text-muted" style="font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.8;">
      AI won't replace your engineers, but it changes what they spend time on.
      Instead of writing every line from scratch, they evaluate, guide, and
      verify what the tools produce. I use AI to speed up delivery and reduce
      cost where it makes sense, but I won't pretend it's a substitute for
      judgment. Done right, it accelerates your timeline. Done badly, it creates
      a mess that costs more to fix than it saved.
    </p>
    <p
      class="m-0 text-muted mt-3"
      style="font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.8;"
    >
      I help teams adopt AI where it actually pays off. That means integrating
      it into their workflows, setting guardrails so output is reviewed rather
      than trusted blindly, and making sure the time saved actually matters
      instead of turning into technical debt.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Notable companies -->
  <section
    class="mb-8"
    style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); padding-top: 1.25rem;"
  >
    <h2 class="m-0 mb-2 text-dim" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">
      Notable companies
    </h2>
    <CompanyCards />
  </section>

  <!-- About me -->
  <section class="pt-5 mb-6" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);">
    <h2 class="m-0 mb-2 text-dim" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">About me</h2>
    <p class="m-0 text-muted" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.8;">
      I've spent the last ten years building software across startups and
      enterprise, from early prototypes to production systems serving real
      users. I've led teams, mentored engineers, and worked independently with
      clients who needed someone they could trust with the technical side of
      their business. I also mentor junior engineers and previously taught
      programming, because I think more people should be able to do this work.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Footer -->
  <footer class="pt-3.5" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);">
    <p class="m-0 text-dim" style="font-size: 0.6875rem;">© Halvard Mørstad</p>
  </footer>
</Layout>
